WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.070
About 800 million people live within
100 kilometres of an active volcano.

2
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.770
Picture a town and its farms
on a volcano's lower slopes,

3
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.270
below the summit.

4
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:14.270
Every one of those volcanoes is active.

5
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.310
Any of them could erupt again.

6
00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.530
So why don't people just move away?

7
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:20.330
Don't they know the danger?

8
00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:25.150
In this mission, you'll uncover the
reasons people choose to stay so close to

9
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:25.510
danger.

10
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:30.870
Then you'll explore hazard maps, which
show where the danger is greatest.

11
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:35.570
Your mission: explain why so many
people stay close to active volcanoes,

12
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:37.330
instead of moving away.
